windowtext;padding:0cm\">Id   A   \r\nB    C  total<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" dir=\"LTR\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;direction:ltr;unicode-bidi:embed;background-image:initial;background-size:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:&#39;Courier New&#39;;border:1pt none windowtext;padding:0cm\">3    11   4   \r\n7   22<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" dir=\"LTR\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;direction:ltr;unicode-bidi:embed;background-image:initial;background-size:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:&#39;Courier New&#39;;border:1pt none windowtext;padding:0cm\">4    9    7   \r\n8   24<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" dir=\"LTR\" style=\"direction:ltr;unicode-bidi:embed\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" dir=\"LTR\" style=\"direction:ltr;unicode-bidi:embed\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;line-height:107%;font-family:&#39;Courier New&#39;;border:1pt none windowtext;padding:0cm\">I was able to do so for one\r\ncolumn with:<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" dir=\"LTR\" style=\"direction:ltr;unicode-bidi:embed\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;line-height:107%;font-family:&#39;Courier New&#39;;border:1pt none windowtext;padding:0cm\">df.grouped&lt;- aggregate(df$A~Id,\r\ndata=df, FUN=&quot;sum&quot;)<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" dir=\"LTR\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;direction:ltr;unicode-bidi:embed;background-image:initial;background-size:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:&#39;Courier New&#39;;border:1pt none windowtext;padding:0cm\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" dir=\"LTR\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;direction:ltr;unicode-bidi:embed;background-image:initial;background-size:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:&#39;Courier New&#39;;border:1pt none windowtext;padding:0cm\">I have many columns (A-Z), so I need some kind\r\nof loop. I tried:<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" dir=\"LTR\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;direction:ltr;unicode-bidi:embed;background-image:initial;background-size:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:&#39;Courier New&#39;;border:1pt none windowtext;padding:0cm\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" dir=\"LTR\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;direction:ltr;unicode-bidi:embed;background-image:initial;background-size:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:&#39;Courier New&#39;;border:1pt none windowtext;padding:0cm\">df.grouped&lt;- aggregate(df[4:51]~Id, data=df,\r\nFUN=&quot;sum&quot;)<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" dir=\"LTR\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;direction:ltr;unicode-bidi:embed;background-image:initial;background-size:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:&#39;Courier New&#39;;border:1pt none windowtext;padding:0cm\">names(df.grouped)&lt;-paste(names(df)[4:51])<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" dir=\"LTR\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;direction:ltr;unicode-bidi:embed;background-image:initial;background-size:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:&#39;Courier New&#39;;border:1pt none windowtext;padding:0cm\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" dir=\"LTR\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;direction:ltr;unicode-bidi:embed;background-image:initial;background-size:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:&#39;Courier New&#39;;border:1pt none windowtext;padding:0cm\">But got:<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" dir=\"LTR\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;direction:ltr;unicode-bidi:embed;background-image:initial;background-size:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:&#39;Courier New&#39;;border:1pt none windowtext;padding:0cm\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" dir=\"LTR\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;word-break:break-all;direction:ltr;unicode-bidi:embed\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:#c5060b;background:#e1e2e5\">Error in\r\nmodel.frame.default(formula = df[4:51] ~ Id, data = df) : <u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" dir=\"LTR\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;word-break:break-all;direction:ltr;unicode-bidi:embed\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:#c5060b;background:#e1e2e5\">  invalid type (list) for variable &#39;df[4:51]&#39;</span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:black;background:#e1e2e5\"><u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" dir=\"LTR\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;direction:ltr;unicode-bidi:embed;background-image:initial;background-size:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:&#39;Courier New&#39;;border:1pt none windowtext;padding:0cm\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" dir=\"LTR\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;direction:ltr;unicode-bidi:embed;background-image:initial;background-size:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:&#39;Courier New&#39;;border:1pt none windowtext;padding:0cm\">As you can see, I also want the names in df.grouped\r\nto be the same as in df.<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" dir=\"LTR\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;direction:ltr;unicode-bidi:embed;background-image:initial;background-size:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:&#39;Courier New&#39;;border:1pt none windowtext;padding:0cm\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" dir=\"LTR\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;direction:ltr;unicode-bidi:embed;background-image:initial;background-size:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:&#39;Courier New&#39;;border:1pt none windowtext;padding:0cm\">Any ideas?<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" dir=\"LTR\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;direction:ltr;unicode-bidi:embed;background-image:initial;background-size:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:&#39;Courier New&#39;;border:1pt none windowtext;padding:0cm\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" dir=\"LTR\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;direction:ltr;unicode-bidi:embed;background-image:initial;background-size:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;fo